  "tarball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/billlza/cfw-rs/tarball/v0.5.1-build.51006",
  "zipball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/billlza/cfw-rs/zipball/v0.5.1-build.51006",
  "body": "## Changes in build 51006\n\n- **Installation identity recovery:** Settings → Installation identity → Recover and restart lets the current macOS account recover after an account change or loss of its local Keychain identity. Recovery requires system authentication and confirmed network Off, preserves the machine's replay history and other accounts' credentials, and restarts the app before connections resume.\n- **Connection diagnostics:** changing routing mode marks earlier results stale, so a new UDP check does not compare with HTTPS observations from the previous mode.\n- **Service upgrades:** retry one refused Global Authority registration after a completed unregister, only after checking that the Tunnel and both services remain Off.\n- **Maintenance updates:** the product version remains 0.5.1. The updater now recognizes higher builds of the same version, verifies the staged application's version and build, and reports an interrupted update accurately after relaunch.\n- **Dependency fixes:** build with Go 1.27.4 and rustix 1.1.6 for GO-2026-6859 and RUSTSEC-2026-0486.\n\nThe complete changes are in the [changelog](https://github.com/billlza/cfw-rs/blob/7a3ba4f18eaa50a1e8601b042a7b6b151ca9e375/CHANGELOG.md).\n\n## Install and update\n\n- **Apple silicon, macOS 15 or later. Product version 0.5.1, build 51006.**\n- **Users on build 51005 must install this build manually once.** Quit Clash for Mac with ⌘Q so its normal network restoration completes, then open `Clash.for.Mac_0.5.1_arm64.dmg` and replace the app in Applications. The old updater cannot offer another build of version 0.5.1.\n- Build 51006 joins the new macOS update feed and can receive later builds of the same product version. The original 51005 release and legacy feed remain available at their original URLs.\n- If macOS requests network-extension approval, complete it in System Settings. The app continues a pending TUN start after approval.\n\n## Scope\n\nConnection Diagnostics marks older results stale when the engine session or routing mode changes. Installation identity recovery updates only the current macOS account. Another account whose lineage later falls behind the machine's replay cursor may need to recover explicitly.\n\n## Verification and corresponding source\n\n- The frozen product commit is `7a3ba4f18eaa50a1e8601b042a7b6b151ca9e375`. Exact-source macOS CI passed all three jobs; Windows CI passed all six jobs.\n- Rust workspace: 1,864 tests; UI: 543 tests; Swift package: 957 tests. Clippy, Xcode target tests and static analysis passed. Release-tool tests and the two environment-specific integration cases passed across CI and the release Mac.\n- The application and DMG are signed with Developer ID, notarized by Apple and stapled. Gatekeeper verification passed. The updater archive is signed, and its macOS manifest names `0.5.1-build.51006`.\n- The owner approved the exact license and corresponding-source closure. Installation and exported migration journals verify the 51005 → 51006 upgrade.\n- On the release Mac, cancellation left the installation lineage unchanged. A fresh successful macOS authentication restarted the app and advanced the existing account to a higher epoch; lost-identity and cross-account cases are covered by regression tests.\n- Installed GA acceptance passed all 12 required checks, including exact DMG identity, signed service and Network Extension operation, real DNS/TCP/UDP packet traffic, rejected high-risk control requests, credential-log scanning, normal quit and network restoration. These checks ran on the release Mac with bounded packet probes. The collector and driver exited successfully, and both evidence instances were stopped.\n- DMG SHA-256: `49d92ffcee6d6d794d4c4a7bc55faab3957601969b2a9a2cbc795a5d39847ba3`.\n- Distribution seal SHA-256: `bc1adf7ba57fedaaac030e89678ca4518c5b56310bca17938e1e3caacade22d7`.\n"
